          "type": "summary_text",
          "text": "Let me analyze the requirements.\n\nState: qFill retained. SensorFault = HighWet & !LowWet (combinational).\n\nFill logic:\n- If SensorFault or Inhibit: Fill = FALSE\n- Else if HighWet: Fill = FALSE\n- Else if !LowWet: Fill = TRUE\n- Else (LowWet & !HighWet, middle): Fill = qFill\n\nWait, let's check P4: middle & !Inhibit -> Fill <-> qFill. Middle = LowWet & !HighWet. SensorFault false. Good.\n\nBut what about middle & Inhibit? Then Fill forced false by Inhibit. State qFill updated... Let's check fault_inhibit test step 3->4: step 2 (index 3) LowWet=true,HighWet=false,Inhibit=true expected Fill false. Step 4 (index 4) LowWet=true,HighWet=false,Inhibit=false expected Fill false. That's middle, retains prior Fill which was false. Good.\n\nNow retained state update: Fill becomes qFill next scan.\n\nLet's design:\n\n```\nSensorFault := HighWet AND NOT LowWet;\n\nIF SensorFault OR Inhibit OR HighWet THEN\n    Fill := FALSE;\nELSIF NOT LowWet THEN\n    Fill := TRUE;\nELSE\n    Fill := qFill;\nEND_IF\n```\n\nWait careful ordering: \"Inconsistent sensors or Inhibit stop filling\", \"High switch stops\", \"Low switch starts\", \"Middle level retains\". \n\nIf !LowWet & !HighWet & !Inhibit & !SensorFault -> Fill TRUE (P3). Good, matches ELSIF NOT LowWet.\n\nIf LowWet & !HighWet & !Inhibit -> middle -> retain. Good.\n\nWhat about LowWet FALSE HighWet FALSE Inhibit TRUE -> first branch false.\n\nLet me check first scan: qFill initially FALSE. Fill initializes FALSE. Actually with first condition handling.\n\nLet's verify hysteresis test:\n- Step0: L=F,H=F,I=F, qFill=F. SensorFault=F. Not fault/inhibit/high. NOT LowWet=T -> Fill=T. ✓\n- Step1: L=T,H=F,I=F, qFill=T. middle -> Fill=qFill=T. ✓\n- Step2: L=T,H=T -> HighWet -> Fill=F. ✓\n- Step3: L=T,H=F, qFill=F -> middle -> F ✓\n- Step4: L=F,H=F, qFill=F -> NOT LowWet -> T ✓\n\nfault_inhibit:\n- Step0: L=T,H=F,I=F,qFill=F -> middle -> F ✓\n- Step1: L=F,H=T -> SensorFault=T, Fill=F ✓\n- Step2: L=F,H=F,qFill=F -> Fill=T ✓ SensorFault=F ✓\n- Step3: L=T,H=F,I=T -> Inhibit -> Fill=F ✓\n- Step4: L=T,H=F,I=F,qFill=F -> middle -> F ✓\n\nGreat.\n\nNow qFill update. Need retained variable stored at end. Use a variable qFill: BOOL, and at end qFill := Fill. But since Fill computed then used next scan, that's fine.\n\nNote: P4 uses qFill = pre-scan retained Fill. Good.\n\nNow declaration:\n\nFUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task\nVAR_INPUT\n  LowWet : BOOL;\n  HighWet : BOOL;\n  Inhibit : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n  Fill : BOOL;\n  SensorFault : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n  qFill : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n\nNo init needed since BOOL defaults FALSE. But specification says Fill initializes FALSE. Add `Fill : BOOL := FALSE;` maybe. In VAR_OUTPUT init allowed? Yes.\n\nImplementation as above, then qFill := Fill.\n\nLet me write."
